  "source": {
    "plan": "Remake of 2026-11-08-tape-action-cut after Canberk's notes (DIRECTION 2026-11-06 01:00): lead with the plain job, self-tape hands free. Say action, it rolls; say cut, it stops and plays the take straight back.",
    "feature": "tape",
    "app": "Ghost Light Tape room, the real app as a web page (ghostlight-web/serve.sh), flow flows/tape-hands-free.json. The scripted ear (tape-ear.web.ts) hands the room the words at the voice-over's times; the real tape-cues.ts decides: a lone 'action' rolls, a lone 'cut' stops. The web preview records the camera with MediaRecorder and keeps the take in memory (takes.web.ts), so the real Review screen plays it straight back. Roll and cut tones are the app's own sounds from the recording.",
    "monologue": {
      "id": 847,
      "character": "Richard",
      "play": "Richard III",
      "author": "William Shakespeare",
      "public_domain": true,
      "sql": "select m.id, m.character_name, p.title, p.author from monologues m join plays p on p.id=m.play_id where m.text ilike 'Now is the winter of our discontent%'",
